comment This file demonstrates all concepts implemented in lkeycpp.

comment 1. Variables and basic I/O
var my_name is "Gemini"
var current_year is 2023

say "Hello, my name is " plus my_name
say "The current year is " plus current_year

comment 2. Math Operations and Reassignment
var num_a is 10
var num_b is 3
say "num_a plus num_b is " plus (num_a plus num_b)
say "num_a minus num_b is " plus (num_a minus num_b)
say "num_a into num_b is " plus (num_a into num_b)
say "num_a div num_b is " plus (num_a div num_b)
say "num_a reminder num_b is " plus (num_a reminder num_b)

num_a is num_a plus 5
say "num_a after reassignment is " plus num_a

comment 3. Input
var user_age is 23
say "You are " plus user_age plus " years old."

comment 4. Conditionals (If-Else If-Else)
var score is 85
when (score greater than 90) then
    say "Excellent!",
when (score greater than 80) then
    say "Very Good!",
when nothing then
    say "Keep trying!".

comment 5. Comparisons and Logic
var is_active is 1 comment true is represented as 1
var has_permission is 0 comment false is represented as 0

when (is_active and not has_permission) then
    say "Active but no permission.",
when nothing then
    say "Either inactive or has permission." .

comment 6. Loops - Range For Loop
say "--- Counting from 1 to 3 ---"
with i from 1 to 3 then
    say "Count: " plus i.

comment 7. Loops - While Loop
say "--- Countdown from 3 ---"
var counter is 3
with (counter greater than 0) then
    say "Counter: " plus counter
    counter is counter minus 1.

comment 8. For-Each Loop (implemented feature)
var sentence is "this is a test sentence"
say "--- Iterating words ---"
with sentence is word as words then
    say word.

say "--- Iterating letters ---"
var short_word is "abc"
with short_word is char as letter then
    say char.

comment 9. Arrays (implemented feature)
say "--- Array Demonstrations ---"
var empty_list is ()
say "Empty list: " plus empty_list

var numbers is (10, 20, 30, (40, 50))
say "Numbers array: " plus numbers
say "First element: " plus numbers(0)
say "Nested element numbers(3)(1): " plus numbers(3)(1)

var mixed_data is (1, "two", 3.0, 1) comment true is represented as 1
say "Mixed data array: " plus mixed_data
say "Second element (string): " plus mixed_data(1)

